{"author":{"id":"1949ffc23f11a8cb4f8c42a45c9ad241b49570df9a18687489e9ea78d87c54a3"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1779166236,"nonce":"4M6hIuQ8bqSL2tN1vfquLsOV9yQ=","message":"## Core Feedbax design orientation after current Studio merges\n\nThe latest Studio work does not close the Feedbax-wide design questions here; it makes several of them more concrete.\n\nWhat is now available on `develop`:\n\n- The Train/Evaluate collection slice (`971a994`) gives Studio a real run/evaluation collection UI over imported RLRMP data.\n- The Scenario Projection Workspace (`0d82869`) gives Studio a shared scenario entity/selection/objective surface instead of separate graph-only and training-form-only ownership.\n\nCore Feedbax contract pressure that remains:\n\n- `c6c6da0`, `f68cf66`, and `e33f487` still need deeper provider/manifest/indexing coverage for evaluation, analysis, reports, schema discovery, extension packages, artifact publication, and import/export. The UI now has richer concepts that should lower into those contracts rather than invent parallel frontend state.\n- `85cec2c` needs backend/runtime introspection, not just frontend widgets: selectors should be able to enumerate structured state paths, array shapes/dtypes, task/mechanics/objective references, and compatibility information that validators can check.\n- `e5a1e6c` needs metric specs/templates to be first-class Feedbax concepts or validated provider outputs, so Studio tables can render task-aware columns without hardcoded RLRMP semantics.\n- `e57ae1f` is still the boundary where Studio scenario/task/objective/stage specs must lower into real JAX training/eval/analysis execution, with manifests and checkpoints tied to exact snapshots.\n\nRecommended design stance: keep the next Studio slices additive to the core contracts. A selector browser, task-aware metrics, and real execution should reuse provider schemas, registries, validators, manifests, and artifact refs where possible instead of becoming another UI-local interpretation layer.\n\n---\nCo-Authored-By: Codex (GPT-5) \u003ccodex@openai.com\u003e","files":null}]}